+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole
+number of seconds, like `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit, like `1h30m`. The units are `d`
+(days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once, in that order. Units are
+case-insensitive, and spaces are not allowed.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration())
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout}")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h 30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
